exercises.solution:
```python
def reduce_tau(tau):
    while True:
        tau -= round(tau.real)
        if abs(tau) < 1 - 1e-15:
            tau = -1 / tau
        else:
            return tau
```

Why it terminates: $\operatorname{Im}(-1/\tau) = \operatorname{Im}\tau/|\tau|^2 > \operatorname{Im}\tau$ when $|\tau| < 1$, and the imaginary parts of the points of an $SL(2, \Z)$-orbit are bounded above with only finitely many values above any given level. The output determines the torus $\C/(\Z + \Z\tau)$ up to biholomorphism — up to the identifications on the boundary of the domain.
